# Local figure-inspection scratch pages
.fig_*.html

# Reference PDF corpus: a local working library, not a repository asset.
# PDFs are never tracked - cite them by DOI in references/reference_index.md
# instead. The eight that predated this rule were purged from history on
# 2026-08-09 (git filter-repo), removing ~107 MB; scripts/check_repo_integrity.py
# now rejects any tracked PDF with no exceptions.
references/*.pdf

# Kearns-parameter reference corpus: vendor PDFs plus several MB of raw XRDML
# instrument data, used as a local source for tutorial 31 and never a repository
# asset. Cite the papers by DOI in references/reference_index.md instead.
kearns_parameter_data_references/

# Everything above serves one cardinal rule, stated in AGENTS.md under
# "Repository content: sources and canonical assets only": if a command in this
# repository can regenerate a file, it is committed only when documentation, a
# test, a manifest, or a pinned baseline refers to it by name. Add the entry here
# before or in the commit that first produces the artifact - history is permanent,
# so a stray committed once is carried by every clone forever.
